{"explanation":"If you compound n times a year at 100% interest, your $1 becomes (1 + 1/n)^n dollars. With n=1 you get $2, with n=2 you get $2.25, monthly gives about $2.613, and daily about $2.7146. The growth doesn't blow up. It levels off at e ≈ 2.71828, even if you compound continuously. Drag the slider to change n and watch the dot climb toward the dashed line at e.","manimCode":"const axes = new Axes({ xRange: [0, 50, 10], yRange: [1.5, 3, 0.5], xLength: 9, yLength: 4.5, tips: false });
axes.moveTo([0, -0.4, 0]);
const f = (n) => Math.pow(1 + 1 / n, n);
const curve = axes.plot(x => f(x), { color: BLUE, xRange: [1, 50], numSamples: 200 });
const eLine = axes.plot(x => Math.E, { color: YELLOW });
scene.add(axes, curve, eLine);

const eLabel = new MathTex({ latex: 'e \\approx 2.71828' });
await eLabel.waitForRender();
eLabel.moveTo([3.8, 2.3, 0]);
scene.add(eLabel);

const title = new MathTex({ latex: '\\left(1+\\frac{1}{n}\\right)^n' });
await title.waitForRender();
title.moveTo([-3.5, 3.2, 0]);
scene.add(title);

const dot = new Dot({ point: axes.c2p(1, 2), color: RED });
scene.add(dot);

let valLabel = new Text({ text: 'n = 1, value = 2.00000', color: WHITE, fontSize: 24 });
valLabel.moveTo([0, -3.6, 0]);
scene.add(valLabel);

const controls = new Controls(scene, { position: 'top-right' });
controls.addSlider({ label: 'n (compounds/year)', min: 1, max: 50, value: 1, step: 1, onChange: (n) => {
  dot.moveTo(axes.c2p(n, f(n)));
  scene.remove(valLabel);
  valLabel = new Text({ text: 'n = ' + n + ', value = ' + f(n).toFixed(5), color: WHITE, fontSize: 24 });
  valLabel.moveTo([0, -3.6, 0]);
  scene.add(valLabel);
}});

await scene.wait(999999);"}

